    \title Turn on \QMLLS

    \l{\QMLLS} offers code completion and issues warnings for QML. \QVSC supports
    \QMLLS from Qt 6.8.0, and later. You can check for \QMLLS updates and
    download the latest version.

    To turn on \QMLLS when you activate an extension:

    \list 1
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
            \uicontrol {Qt: Open Qt Settings}.
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Qt Qml Configuration}, and select
            \uicontrol {Run \QMLLS when activating an extension}.
            \image {vscodeext-qt-settings-qml.webp} {Qt QML Configuration}
    \endlist

    To use custom \QMLLS arguments instead of the default arguments, select
    \uicontrol {Add Item} in \uicontrol {Custom Args} and add the arguments.

    \section1 Check for updates

    To install the latest \QMLLS version, go to \uicontrol {Command Palette},
    and then select \uicontrol {Qt: Check for \QMLLS update}.

    If \QVSC finds a newer version of \QMLLS, it offers to install it.
    You can also go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and then select
    \uicontrol {Qt: Download the most recent \QMLLS language server}.

    To turn off the notification about downloading \QMLLS, go to
    \uicontrol {Qt Qml Configuration} and select
    \uicontrol {Do Not Ask for Qmlls Download}.

    \section1 Set \QMLLS location

    To use \QMLLS when you develop with an older Qt version than Qt 6.8.0, go to
    \uicontrol {Qt Qml Configuration} and set the path to \QMLLS from Qt 6.8.0
    or later in \uicontrol {Custom Exe Path}.

    \section1 Configure \QMLLS output

    To collect trace output from \QMLLS, go to \uicontrol {Qt Qml Configuration}
    and select an option in \uicontrol {Handle LSP trace}.

    To show verbose output from \QMLLS, select \uicontrol {Verbose Output}.

    \section1 Manage QML modules

    To look for QML modules in the specified folders and use the \c {-I}
    option to add import statements for them when you start \QMLLS, go to
    \uicontrol {Qt Qml Configuration} and select \uicontrol {Add Item} in
    \uicontrol {Additional Import Paths}.

    To use the \c {QML_IMPORT_PATH} and \c {-E} options to look for QML modules
    when you start \QMLLS, select \uicontrol {Use QML Import Path Env Var}.

    To stop \QMLLS from triggering a CMake rebuild when it detects that the
    source code of a C++ defined QML type has been modified, select
    \uicontrol {No CMake Calls}. For more information, see
    \l {Disabling Automatic CMake Builds}.

    \section1 Restart \QMLLS

    To restart \QMLLS, go to \uicontrol {Command Palette} and select
    \uicontrol {Qt: Restart \QMLLS}.


    \sa {Qt settings}
*/
